Sval: Ctrl+Tab's list drawn by Sval's switcher

ctrlTab's panel shows at most seven tabs and leaves the rest to the list of
all tabs, which opens from the tab strip Sval removes, so most of a
workspace's tabs were out of reach. Its previews of most pages come from
thumbnail storage (tabPreviews), which Sval turns off
(browser.pagethumbnails.capturing_disabled) and which would write what the
user browses to disk, so those pages showed nothing. ctrlTab keeps its
order and keys, and hands the list to SvalTabSwitcher.sys.mjs, which draws
every tab and captures previews in memory. The list it walks (tabList) adds
the pages of the workspace's pins, which Sval keeps as hidden tabs that
ctrlTab leaves out, and sorts by use, since tabs Sval restores open in the
background, where ctrlTab files each second. While the switcher shows, Ctrl
and the key above Tab step back through it, as Ctrl+Shift+Tab does; closed,
that key is the page's. The panel and tabPreviews, which nothing else uses,
go. ctrlTab.css stays: taking it out of the theme's jar.inc.mn would move
the Gecko key.

